o The chance of vorpal blade beheading should increase by 1% per 1
point of enchantment.  Or some fraction of a % anyway.

o All bees in a beehive should wake up if the queen is attacked

o Ant holes should have a queen too, with similar behaviour to the
last point.

o Partially eating a cockatrice corpse isn't fatal.  It should
be so, instantly.  I started eating, it was "rotten" (although
freshly-killed; but that's another story), so I lost consciousness,
but didn't turn to stone.

o Freshly-killed corpses *can't* be rotten!  If we must have this
effect, CALL IT SOMETHING ELSE!

o All quest artifacts should grant magic resistance.

o Carried garlic should scare vampires.  Eaten garlic should have
the same effect for n turns after the eating.  More to the point,
they shouldn't attack you at all -- at the moment, they still can
even though scared (though maybe this has something to be with your
being invisible/displaced?  Hmm...)

o States of burdened, stressed etc should have negative impact on
dexterity -- 1 per?

o Conversely, dexterity should give a bonus to AC á la slashem

o Protection should only be purchasable from a priest of one's own
alignment -- why would a hostile God give you help?

o Ravens should be peaceful for Valkyries (Odin's special bird)

o Greasing of armour items should affect the probability that succubi
can remove them (appropriate message); with usual probability that
the grease wears off.

o Trollsbane should do something *useful*!  ditto Ogresmasher,
Werebane, Dragonbane, Demonbane.  e.g. Sunsword's permanent light
function.

o Guarantee each class as first gift from sacrifice, a *decent*
artifact weapon -- it doesn't have to be spectacular, just *not*
useless shit like Trollsbane!

o A Monk should get a positive alignment adjustment for not eating
until weak, or fainting.

